{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834080-penalty-dice","id":834080,"title":"Penalty dice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-20T15:15:42-08:00","id":834080,"title":"Penalty dice","content":"never mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","user":"granite","date":". 06-19-2016, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","name":"granite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T18:19:01-08:00","id":834170,"title":"","content":"I've never really had much problems with negative modifiers being forgotten, but as a ST/GM regardless of game, I tend to be a bit of a hardass about people rolling before a roll is called for. This came out of a lot of time introducing people that had only played d20 with certain mutual acquaintances and where used to rolling things like Spot checks preemptively because of their style of GMing. Players can roll dice all they want. I only pay attention to rolls after they've told me what their character is trying to do, and I've had a chance to consider (1) if they even need to roll, (2) if so what, and (3) modifiers.<br /> <br /> As for the math side of things, the mean successes of (X-Y) dice, and X dice - Y dice is the same. However the variance increases with this method, meaning your odds of doing worse and better than average increase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:17:58-08:00","id":834216,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think it is generally better to go with a simpler solution were one is available.<br /> <br /> In this case, I refer to the solution of simply letting any mistake about how many dice were meant to be rolled slide since getting the rules right is not a high enough priority in the group for you and your group to have gotten into the practice of tallying all bonuses and penalties prior to picking up their dice.<br /> <br /> As for some of the other questions asked, I'll give some answers and advice:<br /> <br /> Firstly, if you want actually condition your group to get the rules right, start making sure you say things like &quot;Roll Strength and Brawl, minus 3&quot; and that your players never touch their dice until you've explained what they are going to be rolling - especially useful to that end is to tell your players not to phrase things as die rolls (i.e. &quot;I'm going to roll larceny on this locked door.&quot;), but as intended actions to which you might simply reply &quot;you succeed&quot; rather than ask for a die roll (i.e. &quot;I'm going to try picking the lock on this door.&quot;).<br /> <br /> Secondly, if the dice have already hit the table and the player has rolled more than appropriate, a thing that can be done - and will likely result in the player developing the desire to make sure their dice pool is correct before rolling in the future - is to ignore that roll entirely, and re-roll with the corrected number of dice. The players all having their time wasted each time one of them rolls before asking which if any bonuses or penalties apply is a very strong motivator, in my experience, for everyone to start working together to prevent future wasted time. It is how my group got used to the then new idea of altering the number of dice rather than the target number when we changed over to Vampire: the Requiem back in the day.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if you and your group find it more fun to use penalty dice, forget the math-side of things - the math doesn't at all matter if fun is being had, which is the entire reason for my suggested simpler solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T06:33:54-08:00","id":834395,"title":"","content":"never mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","user":"granite","date":". 06-19-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","name":"granite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T06:48:03-08:00","id":834398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>granite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834080-penalty-dice?p=834395#post834395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I'm only looking for input regarding the probabilities with this method. I specifically don't want to discuss pros and cons of various approaches to handling mistake corrections, I just wanted to provide some context.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, that's interesting. Sounds like a positive change too, as far as I'm concerned. However, it didn't really feel that way in play, at least it wasn't obvious enough for anybody to notice and voice it. How substantial would you say the increase in variance should this method actually produce?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a lack of discipline on both sides.Dicepools are different than single dice rolls. Try building a Wod THaC0 chart to help you. Only the # is # of dice not the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T07:36:38-08:00","id":834422,"title":"","content":"never mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","user":"granite","date":". 06-19-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","name":"granite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T08:18:18-08:00","id":834436,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: I'm not, you know, an accredited mathmagician or whatever.<br /> <br /> In Chronicles of Darkness, 8-10s are successs, 10s explode, and so on. This translates, roughly, into a number of successes equal to a third of the number of dice rolled, on average.<br /> <br /> The &quot;negative&quot; dice, then, would cancel out a success one in three times.<br /> <br /> As some rough math, let's compare a dice pool of 20, with 10 additional negative dice (so thirty dice, total) vs. a dicepool of 10 (20 dicepool with a penalty of 10 dice, specifically).<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness dicepool's average result is ~3 successes, in that example.<br /> <br /> Houserule dicepool's average result is also ~3. 20 &quot;positive&quot; dice generate an average of ~6 successes, the 10 &quot;negative&quot; dice generate and average of ~3 successes. ~6 - ~3 = ~3.<br /> <br /> (as a sidenote, in case I look like an asshole for this format, I'm actually working through this as I type. Not doing some weird, shitty version of the Socratic Method or something).<br /> <br /> So, as far as I can tell, your houserule works just fine. Other than Dramatic Failures, as you mentioned, but you could probably make something up for that. Harken back to Classic World of Darkness and say that if there's more &quot;negative&quot; successes than &quot;positive&quot; successes, and you have &quot;positive&quot; dice with 1's showing, it's a dramatic failure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T09:05:26-08:00","id":834453,"title":"","content":"never mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","user":"granite","date":". 06-19-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","name":"granite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T09:18:10-08:00","id":834458,"title":"","content":"One difference I can see is that by RAW there's no difference between a penalty equal to your dice pool and one that is several dice above it, leaving you in negatives. Here there is. The probability of success doesn't level off at 10%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:19:53-08:00","id":834555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>granite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834080-penalty-dice?p=834395#post834395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that's interesting. Sounds like a positive change too, as far as I'm concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, however it means the &quot;expected&quot; results are less reliable. You're also making the odds of failure, and exceptional success, much more opaque. The value of mechanics that trade dice for bonuses to the effect of your attack (such as -3 dice to attack for +1 damage) is now harder to weigh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How substantial would you say the increase in variance should this method actually produce? </div> </div> </div>Variance scales with both the base dice-pool and the negative dice-pool. For this I'll be using standard deviation as a metric for variance (if you need that explained, I can, but the basic reasoning is that it lets me express variance in expected successes instead of a more accurate assessment of statistical variation).<br /> <br /> For example, the standard deviation of 2 dice - 1 dice, is 1.1. Which means you have a ~68% chance of results being between -1.1 and +1.1 of the mean, and 95% chance of results between between -2.2 and +2.2 of mean.<br /> <br /> With 20 dice - 19 dice, the standard deviation jumps to 2.86.<br /> <br /> The standard deviation for just 1 die is 0.73. So for a small dice pool, and a small negative dice pool, you're unlikely to psychologically notice the statistical impact because it will require a very large number of rolls to play out (and humans are generally very poorly designed to track such things). With bigger dice-pools and penalty pools, the impact with be more substantial. You're going to notice a nearly four times higher standard deviation in play quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T03:47:32-08:00","id":842939,"title":"","content":"never mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","user":"granite","date":". 06-19-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10170-granite","name":"granite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T14:45:16-07:00","id":1140909,"title":"","content":"Making a search to find this topic where the OP deliberatelly delete the exchange.<br /> have this person been banned? It would be deserved","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11801-timil","name":"Timil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T22:02:56-07:00","id":1140984,"title":"","content":"Banned users have the word &quot;Banned&quot; replace the word &quot;Member&quot; under their name. I have no idea why they deleted virtually all their public posts. But it was over years ago... so why it happened doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> Also, it's kind of not cool to say someone should be banned because they deleted seven of their posts and long silent threads (they deleted their posts 3 months after nobody responded). If something they said troubled you... report it (as little of a point there is now). The mods can see what the text was before it was edited if that's important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}